    },
    {
      "text": "NOP (Oct 25, 2021): site is 906-950 Monroe Street and 1341 Homestead Road, northwest corner of Monroe Street and Homestead Road, APNs 269-20-095, 269-20-087, 269-20-086; requests General Plan Amendment and rezoning from Historic Combining, General Office and Community Commercial to Planned Development. City contact Associate Planner Steve Le.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-003384"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "SFYIMBY (Apr 2021): plans included relocating two historic houses at 906 and 930 Monroe; site 38,217 sq ft. Draft EIR (Oct 2022): existing residences fronting Monroe Street and Homestead Road retained in place; one basement parking level accessed from Franklin Street; building about 90 feet tall, 72,000 sq ft.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-003383",
        "SRC-003387"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Silicon Valley Voice (Aug 23, 2023): Planning Commission supported the project; Historic Landmarks Commission and Downtown Community Task Force opposed it; City Council voted 4-1 to defer the item to an uncertain date so the applicant could adjust the project. Three to six stories, three historic homes remain in the footprint.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-003385"
      ]
    },
